Grammar

    0 $accept: program $end

    1 program: statements

    2 statements: statement
    3           | statements statement

    4 statement: stmt_e
    5          | stmt_l

    6 stmt_e: FUNC_E '(' uint8_hex ',' uint8_hex ')'

    7 uint8_hex: NUMERIC_STR

    8 num: NUMERIC_STR

    9 $@1: ε

   10 stmt_l: FUNC_L '(' $@1 stmt_l_tail

   11 stmt_l_tail: uint8_hex_seq ')'
   12            | num ',' uint8_hex_seq ')'

   13 uint8_hex_seq: uint8_hex
   14              | uint8_hex_seq uint8_hex


Terminals, with rules where they appear

    $end (0) 0
    '(' (40) 6 10
    ')' (41) 6 11 12
    ',' (44) 6 12
    error (256)
    NUMERIC_STR <yytext_dup> (258) 7 8
    FUNC_E (259) 6
    FUNC_L (260) 10


Nonterminals, with rules where they appear

    $accept (9)
        on left: 0
    program (10)
        on left: 1
        on right: 0
    statements (11)
        on left: 2 3
        on right: 1 3
    statement (12)
        on left: 4 5
        on right: 2 3
    stmt_e (13)
        on left: 6
        on right: 4
    uint8_hex <uint8> (14)
        on left: 7
        on right: 6 13 14
    num <ulong> (15)
        on left: 8
        on right: 12
    stmt_l (16)
        on left: 10
        on right: 5
    $@1 (17)
        on left: 9
        on right: 10
    stmt_l_tail (18)
        on left: 11 12
        on right: 10
    uint8_hex_seq (19)
        on left: 13 14
        on right: 11 12 14


State 0

    0 $accept: • program $end
    1 program: • statements
    2 statements: • statement
    3           | • statements statement
    4 statement: • stmt_e
    5          | • stmt_l
    6 stmt_e: • FUNC_E '(' uint8_hex ',' uint8_hex ')'
   10 stmt_l: • FUNC_L '(' $@1 stmt_l_tail

    FUNC_E  shift, and go to state 1
    FUNC_L  shift, and go to state 2

    program     go to state 3
    statements  go to state 4
    statement   go to state 5
    stmt_e      go to state 6
    stmt_l      go to state 7


State 1

    6 stmt_e: FUNC_E • '(' uint8_hex ',' uint8_hex ')'

    '('  shift, and go to state 8


State 2

   10 stmt_l: FUNC_L • '(' $@1 stmt_l_tail

    '('  shift, and go to state 9


State 3

    0 $accept: program • $end

    $end  shift, and go to state 10


State 4

    1 program: statements •  [$end]
    3 statements: statements • statement
    4 statement: • stmt_e
    5          | • stmt_l
    6 stmt_e: • FUNC_E '(' uint8_hex ',' uint8_hex ')'
   10 stmt_l: • FUNC_L '(' $@1 stmt_l_tail

    FUNC_E  shift, and go to state 1
    FUNC_L  shift, and go to state 2

    $default  reduce using rule 1 (program)

    statement  go to state 11
    stmt_e     go to state 6
    stmt_l     go to state 7


State 5

    2 statements: statement •

    $default  reduce using rule 2 (statements)


State 6

    4 statement: stmt_e •

    $default  reduce using rule 4 (statement)


State 7

    5 statement: stmt_l •

    $default  reduce using rule 5 (statement)


State 8

    6 stmt_e: FUNC_E '(' • uint8_hex ',' uint8_hex ')'
    7 uint8_hex: • NUMERIC_STR

    NUMERIC_STR  shift, and go to state 12

    uint8_hex  go to state 13


State 9

    9 $@1: ε •
   10 stmt_l: FUNC_L '(' • $@1 stmt_l_tail

    $default  reduce using rule 9 ($@1)

    $@1  go to state 14


State 10

    0 $accept: program $end •

    $default  accept


State 11

    3 statements: statements statement •

    $default  reduce using rule 3 (statements)


State 12

    7 uint8_hex: NUMERIC_STR •

    $default  reduce using rule 7 (uint8_hex)


State 13

    6 stmt_e: FUNC_E '(' uint8_hex • ',' uint8_hex ')'

    ','  shift, and go to state 15


State 14

    7 uint8_hex: • NUMERIC_STR
    8 num: • NUMERIC_STR
   10 stmt_l: FUNC_L '(' $@1 • stmt_l_tail
   11 stmt_l_tail: • uint8_hex_seq ')'
   12            | • num ',' uint8_hex_seq ')'
   13 uint8_hex_seq: • uint8_hex
   14              | • uint8_hex_seq uint8_hex

    NUMERIC_STR  shift, and go to state 16

    uint8_hex      go to state 17
    num            go to state 18
    stmt_l_tail    go to state 19
    uint8_hex_seq  go to state 20


State 15

    6 stmt_e: FUNC_E '(' uint8_hex ',' • uint8_hex ')'
    7 uint8_hex: • NUMERIC_STR

    NUMERIC_STR  shift, and go to state 12

    uint8_hex  go to state 21


State 16

    7 uint8_hex: NUMERIC_STR •  [NUMERIC_STR, ')']
    8 num: NUMERIC_STR •  [',']

    ','       reduce using rule 8 (num)
    $default  reduce using rule 7 (uint8_hex)


State 17

   13 uint8_hex_seq: uint8_hex •

    $default  reduce using rule 13 (uint8_hex_seq)


State 18

   12 stmt_l_tail: num • ',' uint8_hex_seq ')'

    ','  shift, and go to state 22


State 19

   10 stmt_l: FUNC_L '(' $@1 stmt_l_tail •

    $default  reduce using rule 10 (stmt_l)


State 20

    7 uint8_hex: • NUMERIC_STR
   11 stmt_l_tail: uint8_hex_seq • ')'
   14 uint8_hex_seq: uint8_hex_seq • uint8_hex

    NUMERIC_STR  shift, and go to state 12
    ')'          shift, and go to state 23

    uint8_hex  go to state 24


State 21

    6 stmt_e: FUNC_E '(' uint8_hex ',' uint8_hex • ')'

    ')'  shift, and go to state 25


State 22

    7 uint8_hex: • NUMERIC_STR
   12 stmt_l_tail: num ',' • uint8_hex_seq ')'
   13 uint8_hex_seq: • uint8_hex
   14              | • uint8_hex_seq uint8_hex

    NUMERIC_STR  shift, and go to state 12

    uint8_hex      go to state 17
    uint8_hex_seq  go to state 26


State 23

   11 stmt_l_tail: uint8_hex_seq ')' •

    $default  reduce using rule 11 (stmt_l_tail)


State 24

   14 uint8_hex_seq: uint8_hex_seq uint8_hex •

    $default  reduce using rule 14 (uint8_hex_seq)


State 25

    6 stmt_e: FUNC_E '(' uint8_hex ',' uint8_hex ')' •

    $default  reduce using rule 6 (stmt_e)


State 26

    7 uint8_hex: • NUMERIC_STR
   12 stmt_l_tail: num ',' uint8_hex_seq • ')'
   14 uint8_hex_seq: uint8_hex_seq • uint8_hex

    NUMERIC_STR  shift, and go to state 12
    ')'          shift, and go to state 27

    uint8_hex  go to state 24


State 27

   12 stmt_l_tail: num ',' uint8_hex_seq ')' •

    $default  reduce using rule 12 (stmt_l_tail)
